{"module":"Term 1","title":"Unit 1 — Personal Relations","description":"Introducing yourself, describing people, present simple vs present continuous.","intro":"This unit is about people around us: family, friends and how to describe them.","objectifs":["Introduce yourself and others.","Describe personality and appearance.","Use the present simple and the present continuous correctly."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary: describing people","h":"<table><tr><th>Personality</th><th>Appearance</th><th>Relations</th></tr><tr><td>friendly, shy, generous, honest, selfish, hard-working</td><td>tall, short, slim, curly / straight hair</td><td>relative, cousin, neighbour, classmate, close friend</td></tr></table>"},{"t":"Grammar: present simple vs present continuous","h":"<ul><li><b>Present simple</b> — habits, facts: <i>She <b>lives</b> in Fes. He <b>plays</b> football every Sunday.</i> Third person singular adds <b>-s / -es</b>.</li><li><b>Present continuous</b> (am / is / are + verb-ing) — actions happening now or temporary: <i>Look! They <b>are playing</b>.</i></li><li>Key words: always, usually, every day → simple ; now, at the moment, look! → continuous.</li></ul><div class=\"box note\"><span class=\"box-title\">Stative verbs</span><p>Verbs like <i>like, know, want, believe, understand</i> are not normally used in the continuous: <i>I <b>know</b> him</i> (not “I am knowing”).</p></div>"},{"t":"Communication: introducing people","h":"<ul><li>“Hi, I’m Sara. Nice to meet you.” — “Nice to meet you too.”</li><li>“Let me introduce my friend Adam.” / “This is my cousin, Yassine.”</li><li>“What does she look like?” (appearance) vs “What is she like?” (personality)</li></ul>"},{"t":"Writing tip: a short profile","h":"<p>Start with name and age, then appearance, personality and hobbies. Use linking words: <i>and, but, also, because</i>.</p>"}],"recap":"Present simple = habits and facts (he plays); present continuous = now / temporary (he is playing). “What is she like?” asks about personality; “What does she look like?” asks about appearance.","cards":[["Present simple","Habits & facts — she <b>works</b>"],["Present continuous","Now — she <b>is working</b>"],["What is he like?","Asks about <b>personality</b>"],["Stative verbs","know, like, want… → no -ing"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"She ___ to school every day.","choices":["goes","go","is going","going"],"answer":0,"explain":"Habit + third person singular → present simple with -es.","why":[null,"With “she” we add -s/-es.","“Every day” shows a habit, not an action happening now.","A verb-ing alone cannot be the main verb."]},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: Look! The children ___ (play) in the garden. (2 words)","accept":["are playing"],"display":"are playing","explain":"“Look!” shows an action happening now → present continuous."},{"type":"qcm","q":"A person who gives a lot to others is…","choices":["generous","selfish","shy","lazy"],"answer":0,"explain":"Generous = happy to give."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"“What is your brother like?” — The best answer is:","choices":["He’s funny and kind.","He’s tall with short hair.","He likes football.","He’s fine, thanks."],"answer":0,"explain":"“What is he like?” asks about personality.","why":[null,"That describes appearance (“What does he look like?”).","That is about hobbies.","That answers “How is he?”."]},{"type":"direct","q":"Correct the verb: “I am knowing your cousin.” → I ___ your cousin.","accept":["know"],"display":"know","explain":"“Know” is a stative verb: no continuous form."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Choose the correct sentence:","choices":["My father usually drinks tea in the morning.","My father is usually drinking tea in the morning.","My father usually drink tea in the morning.","My father drinking tea usually."],"answer":0,"explain":"“Usually” = habit → present simple, with -s for “he”."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Which sentence describes a temporary situation?","choices":["She is staying with her aunt this week.","She lives with her aunt.","She stays with her aunt every summer.","She knows her aunt well."],"answer":0,"explain":"“This week” + continuous = temporary."},{"type":"direct","q":"Write the question for the answer: “He’s tall and slim.” → What does he ___ like? (2 words, missing part)","accept":["look"],"display":"look","explain":"Appearance → “What does he look like?”"},{"type":"qcm","q":"Find the mistake: “Every evening my sister is helping my mother and then she watch TV.”","choices":["is helping → helps ; watch → watches","Every → All","and → but","There is no mistake."],"answer":0,"explain":"“Every evening” is a habit → present simple, and “she” needs -es: helps, watches."}]}}